Why One Attention Head Isn't Enough

Consider:

Kubernetes stores cluster state in etcd.

Different relationships exist simultaneously.

Head 1

May learn:

Kubernetes → etcd

because etcd stores Kubernetes state.

Head 2

May learn grammar:

stores → state
Head 3

May learn subject-object relationships:

Kubernetes → cluster
Head 4

May learn long-range dependencies.

If we had only one head:

One brain

we could only focus on one relationship.

Multi-head attention is like having:

Many brains working in parallel
