Residual Connection (Add)

One of the greatest ideas in deep learning.

Instead of:

Input
 ↓
Attention
 ↓
Output

we do:

Input
 ↓
Attention
 ↓
+
Input
 ↓
Output

Why?

Because information can flow directly.

Without residual connections:

Deep networks become unstable.

Example:

Input:

[1 2 3]

Attention output:

[0.5 1 0.5]

Final:

[1.5 3 3.5]
Layer Normalization

After addition:

Normalize values.

Purpose:

Stabilize training
Prevent exploding values
Speed up convergence
